Functions \( f_{0}, f_{1}, f_{2}, \cdots \) are recursively defined as follows:
1. \( f_{0}(x) = x, x \in \mathbf{R} \);
2. \( f_{2k+1}(x) = 3^{f_{k}(x)}, x \in \mathbf{R}, k = 0, 1, 2, \cdots \);
3. \( f_{2k}(x) = 2^{f_{k-1}(x)}, x \in \mathbf{R}, k = 1, 2, \cdots \).

Which is larger, \( f_{10}(1) \) or \( f_{9}(2) \)? Prove your conclusion.

Solve the system of equations:
\[
\begin{cases}
\frac{1}{x} + \frac{1}{y+z} = \frac{6}{5}, \\
\frac{1}{y} + \frac{1}{x+z} = \frac{3}{4}, \\
\frac{1}{z} + \frac{1}{x+y} = \frac{2}{3}
\end{cases}
\]

\[
\left\{\begin{array}{l}
5 \sqrt{x^{2}-3 y-88}+\sqrt{x+6 y}=19 \\
3 \sqrt{x^{2}-3 y-88}=1+2 \sqrt{x+6 y}
